From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Accept the sampler heap of render and
 compute commands

The G16 SUBMIT check refused every render and compute command that named
a sampler heap. Mesa names one whenever a shader uses a bindless sampler:
honeykrisp lowers every descriptor-set sampler on native AGX3 to
bindless_sampler_agx, and gallium names its batch heap whenever it has
one. So nearly every textured draw or dispatch was refused with EINVAL.

Admit the heap the way the G17 backend does (command::sampler and the
descriptor sampler fields): at most 1024 samplers, the address and count
both zero or both nonzero, an eight-byte aligned address, and readable
user memory for count * 8 bytes. Write the address, the count and the
count plus one (zero without samplers) into the firmware records.

The 25G83 G16 records have no captured sampler fields, so their offsets
are taken from the G17 descriptors by alignment:

  - compute: the G16 compute record is the G17 ComputeDescriptor shifted
    down by 0x740. Its 0x1a440 value (0x7c8), u32::MAX word (0x7e8),
    preempt/end addresses (0x798/0x7a0) and stamp, auxiliary stamp and
    stamp value (0x800/0x808/0x810) sit at the G17 offsets minus 0x740,
    which places sampler_heap_va (G17 0xf2c) at 0x7ec, the count at
    0x7f4 and the bound at 0x7f8.

  - render: the TA record tail is the G17 TaDescriptor shifted down by
    0x2e. Stamp, auxiliary stamp, stamp value, qid (0x70) and the
    first-kick word (1) sit at the G17 offsets minus 0x2e, and the
    timestamp context cell sits four bytes before the predecessor ID in
    both records, as in compute. That places sampler_heap_va (G17 0x87a)
    at 0x84c, the count at 0x854 and the bound at 0x858. The fragment
    record, as on G17, has none.

None of these words is written by the existing encoders. Because the
offsets are inferred, the new g16_sampler_heap module parameter (default
1) restores the old refusal without a rebuild.

Based on the G17 sampler-heap admission and descriptor fields from
859a5d9632 ("drm/asahi: add the T8140 firmware interface") by
DjDeveloperr <hey@djdev.me>.

Build-tested only. The record offsets are not yet qualified on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit f6fca84553c649e344fea7c049702300fd0fd59d)
